  "onbDisclosureTitle": "How FOKUS blocks apps",
  "@onbDisclosureTitle": {
    "description": "Accessibility disclosure heading (F-10) — calm, trustworthy, no alarm."
  },
  "onbDisclosureBody": "[PLACEHOLDER COPY — requires Prashant's verbatim approval before any release; Google Play policy.]\n\nFOKUS uses Android's accessibility service for one purpose: during a focus session it notices which app comes to the foreground, so it can gently step in when you open an app you chose to block.\n\nFOKUS does not read screen content, does not collect personal data, and never sends anything off your device. Everything stays local.\n\nYou can turn the service off in system settings at any time.",
  "@onbDisclosureBody": {
    "description": "PROMINENT DISCLOSURE BODY — PLACEHOLDER, marked in-string on purpose so it cannot ship unnoticed. Final wording is PM-drafted and approved verbatim by Prashant (Play policy). The consent button must follow this text in reading order."
  },
